{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dire-negative-bunting","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout.py::test_preview_is_complete_while_sync_locks_are_held`\nfails intermittently on `macos-latest` CI with:\n\n    subprocess.TimeoutExpired: Command '[...'/.venv/bin/rebar', 'bridge', 'preview']'\n    timed out after 15 seconds\n\nThe Linux legs pass. The test drives `rebar bridge preview` as a SUBPROCESS while holding sync\nlocks, and bounds it at 15 seconds — a contention test with a hard wall-clock bound, which is\ninherently sensitive to how loaded the runner is.\n\n## Not caused by the change it blocked\n\nIt surfaced on Gerrit 2308 (`fix(llm): run the sync LLM drive off a live loop`), which adds a\nthread-offload guard to the LLM runner. Measured on macOS, same machine, three runs each:\n\n    WITHOUT 2308 : 4.02s  3.61s  3.66s\n    WITH    2308 : 3.82s  3.29s  3.75s\n\nNo difference. The change does not touch this path's cost.\n\n**A caution recorded because I fell into it.** My FIRST measurement with the change read 54.54s\nand I called the regression 'decisive' on that single run. The second read 4.58s. The 54.5s was\ncold-start cost compounded by four subagents loading the box. One timing measurement on a busy\nmachine is not evidence, and I should not have reported it as one.\n\n## Why this is a bug, not a retry\n\nAGENTS.md is explicit that a flaky test is a defect to root-cause, not something to `recheck`\naway. The defect here is the test's design: a 15-second bound on a subprocess whose whole purpose\nis to run under deliberately-induced lock contention. On a runner with less CPU headroom than a\ndeveloper laptop, exceeding it says nothing about correctness.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The 15s subprocess bound is replaced by something that does not fail on a slow runner —\n      a generous bound, a deadline scaled to observed baseline, or an assertion on COMPLETION\n      rather than elapsed time.\n- [ ] The test still fails if `bridge preview` genuinely hangs under contention, which is the\n      property it exists to protect. Mutation-check that.\n- [ ] Root cause is stated: whether macOS is slower on this path for a structural reason, or the\n      bound is simply too tight for CI in general.\n\n## Impact\n\nBlocks unrelated changes at random. It blocked 2308, which is itself the fix for\n`superior-trifling-dunlin` — the P1 preventing signed attestations through the MCP server.","id":"8e48-f0bf-fea5-4c57","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["tests","flake","ci","macos"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_preview_is_complete_while_sync_locks_are_held flakes on loaded macOS CI: 15s subprocess timeout is marginal"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787890603403050001,"uuid":"c440cd5f-d312-4e3f-9b5c-6d6d3d08d484"}